## Answers to your specific questions

**Does GetCluster call GetSettings() or IsInClusterEnabled()?**
`GetCluster` calls `IsInClusterEnabled()` — but only when `server == appv1.KubernetesInternalAPIServerAddr`. It does **not** call `GetSettings()`. There is no reference to `GetSettings()` anywhere in the provided code.

**Does WatchClusters call GetCluster?**
Yes. When in-cluster is enabled, `WatchClusters` calls `db.GetCluster(ctx, appv1.KubernetesInternalAPIServerAddr)` to obtain the local cluster, wrapping any error as `"could not get local cluster: %w"`.

